            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മനസ്സിലായില്ല (manassilāyilla) — \"I didn't understand\", literally \"it didn't come into the mind\": മനസ്സ് (manassŭ), \"mind\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മനസ്സിലായില്ല (manassilāyilla) is \"it did not become in the mind\": Sanskrit manas, \"mind\" (CDIAL 9822), with the place ending, then native āyi, \"became\" (DEDR 333), and illa, \"not\" (DEDR 2559). DEDR 333 compares Sanskrit ām."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mind, and the no that closes it."
